NAME
       lvchange - change the settings of a logical volume (active, read-only)

SYNOPSIS
       lvchange -a y|n VG/LV
       lvchange -p r|rw VG/LV

DESCRIPTION
       lvchange changes attributes of existing logical volumes. The most
       used is activation: an inactive LV has no device file (/dev/VG/LV) and
       cannot be mounted. LVs are activated at boot automatically.

OPTIONS
       -a y|n, --activate y|n
              Activate or deactivate the LV. Unmount it before deactivating.

       -p r|rw, --permission r|rw
              Make the LV read-only or read-write.

EXAMPLES
           umount /data
           lvchange -a n vgdata/lvdata
           lvchange -a y vgdata/lvdata

SEE ALSO
       lvcreate(8), lvs(8), lvdisplay(8), vgchange(8)
